<header><p class="st-kicker">kingdom · Anatolia and the Levant</p><h1 class="st-title">Hasmonean Kingdom</h1><p class="st-meta">140 BCE – 37 BCE · capital Jerusalem</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">The Hasmonean Kingdom, the independent Jewish state founded by the Maccabees, whose victory is still celebrated at Hanukkah.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>In 167 BCE <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/antiochus-iv-epiphanes">Antiochus IV</a> of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/seleucid-empire">Seleucid Empire</a> banned Jewish practices, provoking a revolt led by the priest <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mattathias">Mattathias</a> and his sons, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/maccabees">Maccabees</a>. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/judas-maccabeus">Judas</a> recaptured the Temple in 164 BCE. By 140 BCE his brother <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/simon-thassi">Simon</a> had won full independence and was confirmed as high priest and ruler.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>Hasmonean rulers combined the high priesthood with political power, and from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aristobulus-i">Aristobulus I</a> took the title king. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/john-hyrcanus">John Hyrcanus</a> conquered <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/idumaea">Idumaea</a> and destroyed the Samaritan temple on <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mount-gerizim">Mount Gerizim</a>; <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alexander-jannaeus">Alexander Jannaeus</a> extended the realm across the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/hashemite-kingdom-of-jordan">Jordan</a>. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pharisees">Pharisees</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sadducees">Sadducees</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/essenes">Essenes</a> emerged in this era.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>Civil war between <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hyrcanus-ii">Hyrcanus II</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aristobulus-ii">Aristobulus II</a> invited <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pompey">Pompey</a> of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/roman-republic">Roman Republic</a>, who took <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jerusalem">Jerusalem</a> in 63 BCE. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/antigonus-i-monophthalmus">Antigonus</a> regained the throne with Parthian help in 40 BCE, but Herod captured Jerusalem in 37 BCE, founding the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/herodian-kingdom-of-judea">Herodian Kingdom of Judea</a>.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/hasmonean-kingdom.jpg" alt="Hasmonean Kingdom" width="320" height="408"><figcaption>Image: Effib · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Hasmonean_kingdom.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>140 BCE – 37 BCE</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/2nd-century-bce">2nd century BCE</a> – <a href="/centuries/1st-century-bce">1st century BCE</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>kingdom</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>theocratic</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Jerusalem</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>John Hyrcanus, Alexander Jannaeus, Salome Alexandra</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Judaism</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Hebrew, Aramaic</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/israel">Israel</a>, <a href="/countries/palestine">Palestine</a>, <a href="/countries/jordan">Jordan</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Hasmonean Judea, Hasmoneans, Maccabean state</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=-88&amp;focus=hasmonean-kingdom" aria-label="Hasmonean Kingdom on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="5588 1021 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Hasmonean Kingdom lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M5908 1277L6140 1232M5908 1277L5304 942M5908 1277L5908 1277"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M6140 1232h0M5304 942h0M5908 1277h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5908 1277h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M5908 1277h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Jerusalem. <a href="/atlas?year=-88&amp;focus=hasmonean-kingdom">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></d